WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.341
Hi, I'm Peanut!

00:00:02.341 --> 00:00:06.196
Jev-Omni picks an option from text, images, audio or video, all

00:00:06.196 --> 00:00:07.598
through one small head.

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:13.760
Pictures and sound become tokens through one linear layer each.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.741
One decoder reads everything, and a small head picks the answer.

00:00:19.342 --> 00:00:22.230
Gemma 4 has no vision tower or audio encoder.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:26.081
A flat square of pixels, or a slice of raw samples, goes

00:00:26.081 --> 00:00:27.364
through one linear layer.

00:00:27.784 --> 00:00:31.965
Those tokens join the text prompt, options numbered, in one decoder.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:35.765
The decoder was fine-tuned; the front end is Google's, untouched.

00:00:36.185 --> 00:00:40.375
A head reads the last position: one linear layer to two hundred

00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:43.517
and fifty-six classes, with the unused classes masked away.

00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:48.955
That whole front end is fifty-two million parameters, zero point four four

00:00:48.955 --> 00:00:50.312
percent of the decoder.

00:00:52.775 --> 00:00:56.093
A per-option scorer rates each option on its own, so the list

00:00:56.093 --> 00:00:58.304
is just data and the order can't matter.

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:02.385
Here, class one is whatever comes first in the list, and the

00:01:02.385 --> 00:01:04.216
count is welded into the weights.

00:01:04.216 --> 00:01:05.436
So order can matter.

00:01:05.436 --> 00:01:06.962
That's reasoned, not yet tested.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:12.517
Per the card, text, image and audio land under a hundred milliseconds.

00:01:12.517 --> 00:01:15.680
Sixteen frames of video take five hundred and four.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:21.777
The release's own chart: Jev-Omni at eighty-seven point five seven, Jev at

00:01:21.777 --> 00:01:23.186
ninety point four eight.

00:01:23.186 --> 00:01:24.595
Below, not on par.

00:01:25.015 --> 00:01:27.817
Three chat models sit eleven points above both.

00:01:27.817 --> 00:01:30.969
The chart's real argument is the bottom axis: cost.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:36.210
Four modalities reach one head because the base model already turns

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.614
them all into tokens.

00:01:37.614 --> 00:01:39.719
The decision training was text training.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.603
To recap: tiny linear front ends, one fine-tuned decoder, and the option

00:01:45.603 --> 00:01:47.355
count in the head's weights.

00:01:47.775 --> 00:01:49.833
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:49.833 --> 00:01:50.421
I'm Peanut.

00:01:50.421 --> 00:01:50.715
Bye!
